# Normalize all text to LF in the repo and on checkout (all platforms).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries (do not touch line endings)
*.png binary
# *.ppm — raw P6 byte payload; combined with `* text=auto eol=lf` above
# Windows clones would silently rewrite the binary payload otherwise.
# Goldens migrated to PNG on 2026-05-17 but the rule stays as defense in depth
# for any bootstrapped capture or temp file that gets accidentally committed.
*.ppm binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.bmp binary
*.tga binary
*.dds binary
*.psd binary
*.lib binary
*.dll binary
*.exe binary
*.pdb binary
*.ilk binary
*.exp binary
*.zip binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.eot binary
*.pdf binary
*.wav binary
*.mp3 binary
*.ogg binary
*.uasset binary
*.umap binary
*.udk binary
*.blend binary

# Union merge for the backlog archive only.
# Parallel slices in multi-slice plans (see docs/plans/tooling-process-backlog-sweep.md)
# each PREPEND new "Resolution:" entries to applied.md. Without `merge=union`, the
# parallel prepends conflict and require manual resolution per slice (~5 min × N slices).
# Union concatenates both sides on conflict — correct for prepend, may interleave
# date order. Run `bash agents/scripts/core/sort-applied-md.sh` to restore "Latest first"
# ordering when interleaving is visible.
#
# DELIBERATELY NOT applied to process.md / tooling.md / AGENT_SELF_IMPROVEMENT.md:
# - process.md / tooling.md: parallel branches DELETE different entries (the archive
#   step). Union would WRONGLY preserve both deleted entries. Default 3-way merge
#   is correct; manual resolution required on adjacent deletions.
# - AGENT_SELF_IMPROVEMENT.md: parallel branches MODIFY the same count line with
#   different values. Union would garble the count.
docs/self-improvement/categories/applied.md merge=union
# Rotated monthly partitions of applied.md (rotate-applied-md.sh): same
# append-only shape, same parallel-prepend hazard when two branches rotate.
docs/self-improvement/categories/applied-*.md merge=union

# Union merge for high-conflict APPEND-ONLY shared files written by parallel
# sibling PRs in a campaign / decomposition (PR-16: campaign-sibling-prs-edit-
# shared-plan-doc-thrash + decomposition-prs-serial-conflict-shared-files).
#
# tests/CMakeLists.txt: every new tests/Core/<Unit>.test.cpp PR APPENDS its TU +
# curated link-closure block to the hand-maintained add_executable(SmatchetTests …)
# source list. Parallel test PRs therefore append to the SAME region; without
# union each second-to-merge needs a manual conflict resolution (~5 min × N).
# Union concatenates both sides on conflict — correct for append-only growth.
# CAVEAT: union can interleave two unrelated additions or duplicate a line if both
# sides added the identical entry; the configure-time glob-vs-list guard at the
# bottom of tests/CMakeLists.txt catches a DROPPED test (false-green), and a build
# catches a duplicate/garbled entry — so a union artifact fails loudly, it never
# ships silently. Re-run the build after any union auto-merge of this file.
tests/CMakeLists.txt merge=union

# Plan docs: parallel slices of one plan each APPEND to the § Implementation log /
# § Deviations / § Verification sections (post-ship update, process-rules.md
# § Plan-doc family). Union resolves the append-collision; date/slice interleave
# is cosmetic and acceptable. Scoped to active plans (the churning set); shipped/
# archived plans are stable and keep the default 3-way merge.
docs/plans/active/**/*.md merge=union

docs/high-integrity/portable-purity-baseline.txt text eol=lf
